    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Table&nbsp;7.04</span></strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> Summary of the main features of rhabdoid tumour predisposition syndrome</span></p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Other sources include Hirsch Steffen and Judkins Alexander R.",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 459.9pt; margin-left: 7.1pt; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"613\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 190.85pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"254\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Feature</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.05pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Syndrome characteristics</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 190.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"254\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Syndrome MIM number(s)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">609322, 603254</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 190.85pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"254\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Associated malignant tumours</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.05pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">RTPS1 (<em>SMARCB1</em>): AT/RT and extracranial MRT; extremely rarely epithelioid schwannoma, MPNST, and chondrosarcoma</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">RTPS2 (<em>SMARCA4</em>): small cell carcinoma of the ovary of hypercalcaemic type, AT/RT, extracranial MRT</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 190.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"254\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Associated benign tumours</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Meningioma, benign myoepithelioma, ganglioglioma (RTPS1 only)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 190.85pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"254\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Cancer-related inheritance</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.05pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Autosomal dominant</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Penetrance unknown, presumed very high, especially in RTPS1; disease-causing germline variants are de&nbsp;novo in most cases</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">RTPS1/2 can be detected in 25&ndash;35% of patients with malignant rhabdoid tumours</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 190.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"254\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Chromosome location</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">SMARCB1</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> (22q11.2)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">SMARCA4</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> (19p13.2)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 190.85pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"254\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Protein product&ndash;associated pathway</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.05pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Members of the ATP-dependent SWI/SNF chromatin remodelling complex</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"ParaText\" style=\"margin: 6pt 0cm 12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">AT/RT, atypical teratoid/rhabdoid tumour; MPNST, malignant peripheral nerve sheath tumour; MRT, malignant rhabdoid tumour; RTPS1, rhabdoid tumour predisposition syndrome&nbsp;1; RTPS2, rhabdoid tumour predisposition syndrome&nbsp;2.</span></p>",
